{% import "github-repo-button.njk" as repo %}
{% import "stack-list.njk" as stack %}

<div class="prose">
  <p>Each piece has its own repository and lifecycle. Together they serve the Shellui frontend. The graph below draws the same stack twice: every Shellui service, then the version that uses <a href="https://supabase.com">Supabase</a> for authentication and storage. Files stays in both views.</p>
</div>

<section class="mt-10" aria-labelledby="map-the-stack">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="map-the-stack">Map the stack</h2>
    <p>Pick a stack, then follow one box at a time. Pointing at a box or tabbing to it highlights what that box talks to, and each box title links to its section further down. Every arrow is also written out under the graph.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "architecture-graph.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="what-supabase-replaces">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="what-supabase-replaces">What Supabase replaces</h2>
    <p>The shell and your app stay the same in both views. <code>backend.type</code> and <code>storage.url</code> in <code>shellui.config.ts</code> decide which backend answers.</p>
    <div class="prose-table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Piece</th>
            <th scope="col">Full Shellui stack</th>
            <th scope="col">Shellui + Supabase</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Shell frontend</th>
            <td><code>@shellui/core</code></td>
            <td><code>@shellui/core</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Your app</th>
            <td>Iframe with <code>@shellui/sdk</code></td>
            <td>Iframe with <code>@shellui/sdk</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Sign-in</th>
            <td>identity-service, <code>backend.type: "shellui"</code></td>
            <td>Supabase Auth, <code>backend.type: "supabase"</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Storage calls</th>
            <td>storage-service at <code>/storage/v1/*</code></td>
            <td>Supabase Storage at <code>/storage/v1/*</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Blobs</th>
            <td>S3 or the local filesystem</td>
            <td>Held in your Supabase project</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Files</th>
            <td>Files app via <code>filesUrl</code>, against storage-service</td>
            <td>Same Files app against Supabase Storage</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Admin at <code>/admin</code></th>
            <td>The admin app, set with <code>adminUrl</code></td>
            <td>Registers on a Shellui identity backend only</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Hosting</th>
            <td>hosting-service in your infrastructure; all-in temporary deploy of the Browser group at <a href="https://shellui.app">shellui.app</a></td>
            <td>Same all-in temporary deploy at <a href="https://shellui.app">shellui.app</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Embedded apps never call the storage API directly. They call <code>shellui.storage</code>, the SDK posts to the root shell, and the shell runs the request against <code>storage.url</code> with the signed-in user's token. That indirection is why the same app code works in both views.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="prose mt-16">
  {{ stack.heading("shellui", "Frontend", "shell") }}
  <p>The frontend lives in the shellui monorepo, a TypeScript React runtime. <code>@shellui/core</code> owns navigation, layout modes, themes, i18n, modals, and drawers. <code>@shellui/sdk</code> lets apps in iframes talk to the shell. <code>@shellui/cli</code> scaffolds and serves projects. Any stack can run inside the Shellui iframe.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind", "Workbox", "Roarr", "Sentry"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/shellui") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("identity-service", "Backend", "identity-service") }}
  <p>The default authentication backend is identity-service, a Django API for OAuth (GitHub, Google, Microsoft), JWT sessions, and JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) verification. It ships as a Docker image and is deployed at <a href="https://id.shellui.com">id.shellui.com</a>. You can replace it with Supabase Auth - the shell already supports both.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "django-allauth", "Django REST Framework", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/identity-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/identity-service") }}
  </p>

  {{ stack.heading("admin", "Frontend", "admin") }}
  <p>The admin panel is a Vite + React app embedded in the shell at <code>/admin</code>. It manages users, company access, and operational data, and it reads the same identity-service as sign-in. It is static files currently deployed at <a href="https://admin.shellui.com">admin.shellui.com</a>.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/admin") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("storage-service", "Backend", "storage-service") }}
  <p>The storage-service is a Django API with a Supabase-compatible Storage REST surface at <code>/storage/v1/*</code>. It verifies identity-service JWTs and writes blobs to S3 or the local filesystem. It ships as a Docker image and is deployed at <a href="https://storage.shellui.com">storage.shellui.com</a>. You can replace it with Supabase Storage.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "Django REST Framework", "django-storages", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/storage-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/storage-service") }}
  </p>

  {{ stack.heading("files", "Frontend", "files") }}
  <p>Files is a React file manager app. Set <code>filesUrl</code> and it handles browsing, upload, download, folders, permissions, and share links against storage-service or Supabase Storage. On the full stack it also embeds in the admin iframe. It is static files available at <a href="https://files.shellui.com">files.shellui.com</a>.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["TypeScript", "React", "React Router", "shadcn", "Tailwind"]) }}
  <p>{{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/files") }}</p>

  {{ stack.heading("hosting-service", "All-in temporary deploy", "hosting-service") }}
  <p>The hosting-service is a Django API that deploys the whole Browser group as static files - the shell, your app, and Files - under one temporary URL. It ships as a Docker image in your infrastructure and is available as <a href="https://shellui.app">shellui.app</a>. Use it in either stack while you try the product.</p>
  {{ stack.stackList(["Python", "Django", "Django REST Framework", "django-storages", "Swagger", "ReDoc"]) }}
  <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    {{ repo.githubRepoButton("shellui/hosting-service") }}
    {{ repo.dockerImageButton("shellui/hosting-service") }}
  </p>
</div>
